{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Of Benjamin he said.</b> The phrase ״לְבִנְיָמִן״ (\"of Benjamin\") is the words of Moses, and the word ״אָמַר״ (\"he said\") is the words of Scripture — for otherwise, by what would one understand that it is about Benjamin that he is speaking? And so too ״לְיוֹסֵף״ and ״לִזְבוּלֻן״, etc." "And His saying <b>״יִשְׁכֹּן לָבֶטַח עָלָיו״</b>. The meaning: what is the reason He shall dwell in safety? ״עָלָיו״ — meaning, because of his being the neighbor of the One who dwells in the capital city, for who would dare come after the king?"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:09.155302907Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}